# T013 warning with origin_name: calling a zero-parameter function whose scheme
# carries an explicit typeclass constraint that is disconnected from its return type.
#
# g has annotation [constraint: [a: Comparable] return: Int] with no parameters.
# When [g] is called, instantiate_scheme sets origin_name="g" on the Comparable
# constraint. Since the constraint TypeVar does not appear in the return type Int,
# T013 fires at the call site with the better message citing the origin function name:
#   "argument to `g` has unconstrained type — Comparable constraint will be silently dropped"
#
# T013 also fires at g's definition (annotation-driven, no origin_name), producing the
# fallback "ambiguous type variable" message. Both messages appear; this test checks
# for the call-site message with origin_name.
[
  g: [fn@[constraint: [a: Comparable] return: Int] [] 42]
  result: [g]
]
=== out
Dict({"g": Function(), "result": Int(42)})
=== warn
argument to `g` has unconstrained type
